  "legalAiCitationNotice": "AI outputs may cite public legal sources; verify citations before relying on them.",
  "legalAiOutputDisclaimer": "This content was generated by AI and may be incomplete or outdated. It is for informational purposes only and is not legal advice.",
  "legalAttorneyDisclaimer": "This platform connects you with licensed attorneys but does not provide legal advice. Communications may not be privileged until an attorney-client relationship is established.",
  "legalCookiePolicy": "Cookie Policy",
  "legalDataConsentAuditBody": "DVTech Ventures maintains an audit trail of all consent events (grant, modification, withdrawal), data flows into training pipelines, anonymization certifications, and third-party processor instructions. Tenant administrators can request a consent audit report via the governance settings dashboard. We conduct annual AI ethics and data governance reviews.",
  "legalDataConsentAuditHeading": "9. Audit trail and accountability",
  "legalDataConsentConsumerLink": "Consumer data consent settings (your account settings)",
  "legalDataConsentContactBody": "For questions about AI data processing, consent, or to request a copy of consent records: support@odaflow.com. We aim to respond within 10 business days.",
  "legalDataConsentContactHeading": "11. Contact for AI data enquiries",
  "legalDataConsentCountryDPDPBody": "India (DPDP Act 2023): processing of digital personal data for AI training requires explicit consent from the Data Principal. Consent records are maintained and can be reviewed or withdrawn via your account settings.",
  "legalDataConsentCountryGDPRBody": "EU / UK (GDPR / UK GDPR): automated processing that produces legal or similarly significant effects requires a valid legal basis under Art. 22 GDPR. Umbrella does not make binding automated decisions about users. Where AI analysis influences significant outcomes, users are notified and human review is available.",
  "legalDataConsentCountryHeading": "6. Country-specific requirements",
  "legalDataConsentCountryKenyaBody": "Kenya (Data Protection Act 2019): automated processing and profiling must be disclosed; data subjects have the right to object. Consent for any AI training use is obtained separately and documented.",
  "legalDataConsentCountryUSBody": "United States: CCPA/CPRA users have the right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information. Umbrella does not sell personal information. Sharing data with AI providers for service delivery is not a 'sale' under CCPA. Sensitive personal information is not shared with AI providers without explicit consent.",
  "legalDataConsentDefaultBody": "By default, Umbrella does not use your documents, case descriptions, matter notes, client communications, AI queries, or any other user-submitted content to train, fine-tune, or evaluate AI models. This default applies to all users — consumers, Lawyer Users, and firm tenants — regardless of subscription tier. Firm training consent defaults to off for all tenants and can only be enabled by a tenant administrator.",
  "legalDataConsentDefaultHeading": "1. Default: no training on your data",
  "legalDataConsentDescription": "This policy explains how DVTech Ventures handles your data in relation to AI model training, evaluation, and improvement. It forms part of our overall Privacy Policy.",
  "legalDataConsentFirmLink": "Firm training consent (tenant admin — Lawyer OS settings)",
  "legalDataConsentFormDefaultIs": "Default is",
  "legalDataConsentManageBody": "Consent can be granted or withdrawn at any time via your account settings. Changes take effect immediately for future data processing. Withdrawal does not affect processing carried out before the withdrawal.",
  "legalDataConsentManageHeading": "7. How to manage your consent",
  "legalDataConsentNeverUsedBody": "The following data is never used for AI training under any circumstances, including with opt-in: (a) billing information and payment card data; (b) full client names, national ID numbers, passport numbers, or biometric data without complete anonymization; (c) communications protected by legal professional privilege unless the privilege holder provides explicit written consent; (d) data subject to a legal hold or active litigation; (e) health or medical data; (f) data of users under 18 years of age.",
  "legalDataConsentNeverUsedHeading": "4. Data that is never used for training",
  "legalDataConsentOptInAnonymize": "All opt-in data undergoes anonymization (removal of personal identifiers) and pseudonymization (replacement of names, entities, and case references with synthetic tokens) before entering any training pipeline. Anonymization is verified by automated scanning and, for fine-tuning, manual spot-checks.",
  "legalDataConsentOptInEval": "Model evaluation: redacted samples from your AI interactions are used to test model quality, safety, and accuracy against benchmarks. Samples are reviewed only by authorised DVTech engineers and contracted AI evaluators under NDA.",
  "legalDataConsentOptInFineTune": "Fine-tuning: with admin approval, pseudonymized legal drafts or matter summaries may be included in fine-tuning datasets to improve domain-specific model performance. Fine-tuning datasets require dual-approval by a tenant admin and a DVTech data governance officer.",
  "legalDataConsentOptInHeading": "3. What opt-in enables",
  "legalDataConsentOptInIntro": "If you choose to opt in, you may enable one or more of the following, each independently:",
  "legalDataConsentOptInIntroSection": "If you opt in, you may separately enable:",
  "legalDataConsentOptInPrompt": "Prompt improvement: anonymized patterns from your AI queries are used to improve prompt engineering and reduce hallucinations. No personally identifiable information or case-specific facts are included.",
  "legalDataConsentProvidersBody": "Umbrella routes AI queries to third-party AI providers. For analysis and drafting: OpenAI (GPT models) and DeepSeek. For embeddings and document search: OpenAI. For meeting and voice transcription: Deepgram. These providers process your queries under: (a) zero-data-retention API agreements where available (queries are not used to train provider models); (b) data processing agreements that restrict use to service delivery; (c) appropriate cross-border transfer mechanisms (SCCs for EU/UK; equivalent agreements for other jurisdictions). The specific providers in use for each feature are documented in our subprocessor register available on request.",
  "legalDataConsentProvidersHeading": "5. Third-party AI providers",
  "legalDataConsentRetentionBody": "Anonymized training datasets are retained for the period necessary for model development, typically 24 months from creation. Fine-tuning datasets require explicit re-consent after 12 months. Upon tenant account closure, all training data derived from that tenant's content is purged within 60 days.",
  "legalDataConsentRetentionHeading": "10. Training data retention",
  "legalDataConsentTitle": "Data & AI Consent Policy",
  "legalDataConsentWhatIsTrainingBody": "AI training in this context means using your data — after anonymization and pseudonymization — to improve the accuracy, relevance, or safety of AI models that power Umbrella features. It does not mean sharing identifiable client data with any third party. Training pipelines are operated by DVTech Ventures or its contracted AI providers under data-processing agreements.",
  "legalDataConsentWhatIsTrainingHeading": "2. What AI training means",
  "legalDataConsentWithdrawBody": "You may withdraw your consent at any time via account settings or by emailing support@odaflow.com. Upon withdrawal: (a) no further data from your account will enter any training pipeline; (b) previously anonymized data that has already been incorporated into a trained model cannot be removed from that model (as is technically infeasible with anonymized aggregate data, consistent with GDPR Recital 26); (c) any pending training batches containing your data will be purged within 30 days; (d) you will receive confirmation of withdrawal by email within 5 business days.",
  "legalDataConsentWithdrawHeading": "8. Withdrawal of consent",
  "legalDeleteAccountAppName": "Umbrella Legal AI",
  "legalDeleteAccountContactBody": "Email support@odaflow.com from your registered address. We aim to respond within 10 business days.",
  "legalDeleteAccountContactHeading": "Need help?",
  "legalDeleteAccountDeletedBody": "When your account is deleted, we remove or anonymize: your name, email address, phone number, password, consumer profile, issue-checker cases, uploaded documents, legal reports, AI outputs and usage logs tied to your account, lawyer profile (solo users), marketplace leads, training consent records, and active session tokens.",
  "legalDeleteAccountDeletedHeading": "Data that is deleted",
  "legalDeleteAccountDescription": "Request deletion of your Umbrella Legal AI account and associated personal data on umbrella.okaylegal.ai and the Umbrella mobile app.",
  "legalDeleteAccountFirmBody": "If you belong to a law firm workspace, deleting your personal user account removes your profile and access but may not delete matter or client data held by the firm. Firm administrators should contact support@odaflow.com for tenant-level deletion.",
  "legalDeleteAccountFirmHeading": "Law firm and tenant accounts",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormDescription": "Signed-in users can permanently delete their account below. This action cannot be undone.",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormEmailLabel": "Confirm your email",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormEmailPlaceholder": "you@example.com",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormError": "Unable to delete account. Try again or email support@odaflow.com.",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormHeading": "Delete account now",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormLoading": "Checking sign-in status…",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormMismatch": "Email does not match your account.",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormSignIn": "Sign in to delete your account using the form on this page.",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormSignInButton": "Sign in",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormSubmit": "Delete my account",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormSubmitting": "Deleting…",
  "legalDeleteAccountFormSuccess": "Your account has been deleted. You have been signed out.",
  "legalDeleteAccountOperator": "Operated by DVTech Ventures",
  "legalDeleteAccountPartialBody": "Yes. You can delete individual issue-checker cases, uploaded documents, and AI conversation history from within the app or web dashboard without closing your entire account. Email support@odaflow.com if you need help removing specific data.",
  "legalDeleteAccountPartialHeading": "Delete some data without deleting your account",
  "legalDeleteAccountPrivacyLink": "Privacy Policy",
  "legalDeleteAccountRetainedBody": "Some information may be retained where required by law or for legitimate business needs: billing and tax records (up to 7 years), security and audit logs (up to 12 months), anonymized analytics that cannot identify you, and law firm workspace data if you were a member of a firm tenant (managed by your firm administrator).",
  "legalDeleteAccountRetainedHeading": "Data that may be kept",
  "legalDeleteAccountRetentionBody": "Most personal data is deleted or anonymized within 30 days of a confirmed deletion request. Backup copies containing your data are purged on a rolling basis within 90 days.",
  "legalDeleteAccountRetentionHeading": "Retention period",
  "legalDeleteAccountStep1": "Sign in to Umbrella at umbrella.okaylegal.ai or open the Umbrella Legal AI mobile app with the account you want to delete.",
  "legalDeleteAccountStep2": "Use the deletion form on this page while signed in, or email support@odaflow.com from your registered email address with the subject line \"Account deletion request\".",
  "legalDeleteAccountStep3": "Confirm your account email address. We verify that it matches your signed-in account before processing the request.",
  "legalDeleteAccountStep4": "After confirmation, your account is deactivated immediately. Personal data is deleted or anonymized within 30 days, subject to legal retention requirements described below.",
  "legalDeleteAccountStepsHeading": "How to request account deletion",
  "legalDeleteAccountTitle": "Delete your Umbrella account",
  "legalDisclaimerAINotLawyerBody": "Umbrella's AI systems are large language models trained on general legal corpora. They do not hold practising certificates, cannot appear in court, are not regulated by any bar association or law society, and owe no duty of care to you as a lawyer would. AI Outputs may: contain factual errors or hallucinations; omit material considerations relevant to your specific facts; cite statutes or cases that have been amended, repealed, or overruled; fail to account for recent legislative changes; and misinterpret complex or ambiguous legal questions. You must treat every AI Output as a starting point for inquiry, not a final answer.",
  "legalDisclaimerAINotLawyerHeading": "3. AI is not a lawyer",
  "legalDisclaimerCitationBody": "When Umbrella cites a statute, regulation, rule, or judicial decision, you must independently verify: (a) that the cited source exists; (b) that the citation is accurate (section, subsection, and year); (c) that the source is currently in force and has not been amended or repealed; (d) that the quoted text accurately reflects the source. AI citation errors — including fabricated citations — are a known limitation of all current AI systems. Never rely on a citation in legal proceedings, advice, or filings without independent verification.",
  "legalDisclaimerCitationHeading": "4. Citation accuracy",
  "legalDisclaimerJurisdictionBody": "India: AI analysis is based on central legislation, state acts where specified, and published judicial decisions. It does not account for district court-level practice, local bar customs, or uncodified procedural rules. United States: AI analysis is based on federal law and selected state law. US legal analysis is not a substitute for state-specific licensed counsel. Not available for immigration, criminal defence, or tax matters without verified lawyer review. Kenya: analysis draws on Kenyan statutes, subsidiary legislation, and published High Court and Court of Appeal decisions. It does not account for customary law, magistrate court variations, or unpublished rulings. United Kingdom: analysis covers English and Welsh law. Scots law, Northern Irish law, and devolved matters may differ significantly; seek jurisdiction-specific advice.",
  "legalDisclaimerJurisdictionHeading": "8. Jurisdictional limitations",
  "legalDisclaimerLawyerReviewBody": "Certain Umbrella outputs carry an \"Attorney Reviewed\" badge, indicating that a licensed lawyer on our marketplace has reviewed and approved the content. Even reviewed outputs: (a) reflect the lawyer's opinion at the time of review; (b) do not constitute a formal legal opinion unless accompanied by a signed opinion letter; (c) do not create an attorney-client relationship unless a separate retainer agreement is executed; (d) may become outdated as law changes. The reviewing lawyer is an independent contractor; DVTech Ventures does not guarantee the quality or accuracy of any reviewed output.",
  "legalDisclaimerLawyerReviewHeading": "7. Lawyer-reviewed outputs",
  "legalDisclaimerNoPrivilegeBody": "Communications with Umbrella's AI are not protected by attorney-client privilege or legal professional privilege in any jurisdiction. Do not submit information to the platform that you intend to protect under privilege. If you engage a licensed lawyer through the Umbrella marketplace, privilege may attach to your communications with that lawyer under an executed retainer agreement, but not to your prior AI interactions.",
  "legalDisclaimerNoPrivilegeHeading": "5. No attorney-client privilege",
  "legalDisclaimerNotProvideAdvice": "Guaranteed legal advice or predicted legal outcomes",
  "legalDisclaimerNotProvideHeading": "11. What we do not provide",
  "legalDisclaimerNotProvidePrivilege": "Attorney-client privilege for AI interactions",
  "legalDisclaimerNotProvideProfessional": "Professional indemnity for AI-generated outputs",
  "legalDisclaimerNotProvideRepresentation": "Representation before courts, tribunals, or regulatory bodies",
  "legalDisclaimerNotProvideSubstitute": "A substitute for a licensed, qualified lawyer in your jurisdiction",
  "legalDisclaimerPageDescription": "Important notices about Umbrella's AI-generated legal information, its limitations, and user responsibilities. This disclaimer applies to all products and features offered by DVTech Ventures through the Umbrella platform.",
  "legalDisclaimerPageTitle": "Legal Disclaimer",
  "legalDisclaimerRegulatoryBody": "DVTech Ventures is a technology company, not a regulated legal services provider. We are not authorised by the Solicitors Regulation Authority (UK), the Bar Council of India, the Law Society of Kenya, any US state bar, or any other legal regulatory body to provide legal services. The Umbrella platform does not provide regulated legal activity as defined in the Legal Services Act 2007 (UK) or equivalent legislation in other jurisdictions.",
  "legalDisclaimerRegulatoryHeading": "9. Regulatory status",
  "legalDisclaimerRelianceBody": "You acknowledge that: (a) you will not rely solely on AI Outputs to make decisions that affect your legal rights or obligations; (b) you will seek independent qualified legal advice before commencing, defending, or settling legal proceedings; (c) DVTech Ventures is not liable for any harm arising from your reliance on AI Outputs without independent verification. This limitation applies to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.",
  "legalDisclaimerRelianceHeading": "6. Limitation on reliance",
  "legalDisclaimerScopeBody": "This disclaimer applies to every feature of the Umbrella platform, including but not limited to: the Legal Issue Checker, AI Copilot, document review, legal research, matter analysis, strategy memos, draft documents, and any other AI-generated content. It applies to all users — consumers, Lawyer Users, and law firm tenants — across all jurisdictions in which Umbrella operates (India, United States, Kenya, and the United Kingdom).",
  "legalDisclaimerScopeHeading": "1. Scope of this disclaimer",
  "legalDisclaimerUniversalBody": "Umbrella provides legal information, document explanation, issue spotting, and risk analysis. It is not a law firm and does not replace a licensed lawyer. For legal advice specific to your situation, consult a qualified lawyer in your jurisdiction. AI-generated content is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice, legal representation, or the formation of an attorney-client relationship between you and DVTech Ventures.",
  "legalDisclaimerUniversalHeading": "2. Universal disclaimer",
  "legalDisclaimerUserResponsibilitiesBody": "By using the platform you accept responsibility for: (a) evaluating the accuracy and applicability of AI Outputs to your specific situation; (b) obtaining independent legal advice where appropriate; (c) ensuring that your use of AI Outputs complies with your professional obligations (Lawyer Users); (d) not submitting third-party confidential information without authorisation; (e) keeping your account credentials secure.",
  "legalDisclaimerUserResponsibilitiesHeading": "10. User responsibilities",
