  "legalPrivacyAutomatedBody": "Umbrella uses AI to generate legal analysis, identify issues, and suggest actions. These AI outputs are informational only and do not constitute binding decisions about your legal rights. No fully automated decision with legal or similarly significant effect is made about you without human review. Our AI risk-scoring for fraud detection may affect platform access; you may request human review of any such decision.",
  "legalPrivacyAutomatedHeading": "11. Automated decision-making",
  "legalPrivacyChangesBody": "We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be notified by email and in-app notification at least 30 days before they take effect. Continued use of the platform after the effective date constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.",
  "legalPrivacyChangesHeading": "13. Changes to this policy",
  "legalPrivacyChildrenBody": "Umbrella is not directed at persons under 18 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has submitted data to us, contact support@odaflow.com and we will delete it promptly.",
  "legalPrivacyChildrenHeading": "8. Children",
  "legalPrivacyCollectAccountBody": "Account data: email address, full name, phone number (optional), country of residence, and password hash. For lawyer users: bar registration number, firm name, practice areas, and jurisdiction.",
  "legalPrivacyCollectBillingBody": "Billing data: subscription plan, payment method type (card brand, last four digits), billing address, and transaction history. Full payment card details are handled by our PCI-DSS-compliant payment processor (Stripe) and are never stored on our servers.",
  "legalPrivacyCollectContentBody": "Content data: legal documents, case descriptions, matter notes, client communications, and AI-generated outputs that you create or submit through the platform. This content is processed to deliver the service and is not used for AI training without your explicit opt-in.",
  "legalPrivacyCollectCookiesBody": "Cookies and tracking: we use strictly-necessary session cookies, functional preference cookies, and — with your consent — analytics cookies (Vercel Analytics, Sentry error tracking). You may manage cookie preferences via the cookie settings panel.",
  "legalPrivacyCollectDeviceBody": "Device and technical data: IP address, browser type, operating system, device identifiers, screen resolution, and timezone. Used for security, fraud prevention, and service compatibility.",
  "legalPrivacyCollectHeading": "3. Information we collect",
  "legalPrivacyCollectUsageBody": "Usage data: pages visited, features used, AI queries submitted, documents uploaded, time spent, click events, and session recordings (where consent is given). This data is collected via first-party analytics.",
  "legalPrivacyContactBody": "Data protection enquiries: support@odaflow.com. We aim to respond within 10 business days. If you are unsatisfied with our response you have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority: UK — ICO (ico.org.uk); EU — your national DPA; India — Data Protection Board of India; Kenya — Office of the Data Protection Commissioner (odpc.go.ke).",
  "legalPrivacyContactHeading": "14. Contact us",
  "legalPrivacyControllerBody": "Umbrella is operated by DVTech Ventures (\"we\", \"us\", \"our\"). We act as the data controller for information collected from consumers and as a data processor for information held on behalf of law firm tenants. Registered address and data-protection contact: support@odaflow.com. For GDPR purposes, our EU/UK representative can be contacted at the same address.",
  "legalPrivacyControllerHeading": "1. Who we are",
  "legalPrivacyCookiesBody": "Strictly necessary cookies (session management, security tokens) are always active. Functional cookies (language preference, theme) are set on first use and can be cleared in browser settings. Analytics cookies (Vercel, Sentry) are set only with your consent via the cookie banner. We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.",
  "legalPrivacyCookiesHeading": "12. Cookies",
  "legalPrivacyDescription": "How Umbrella collects, uses, and protects your information. This policy applies to all users of umbrella.okaylegal.ai and related Umbrella applications across India, the United States, Kenya, and the United Kingdom.",
  "legalPrivacyLegalBasisBody": "We process personal data under the following legal bases depending on your jurisdiction: (a) Contract — processing necessary to deliver services you have signed up for; (b) Legitimate interests — fraud prevention, platform security, product improvement; (c) Consent — AI training, marketing emails, cookies beyond strictly necessary; (d) Legal obligation — compliance with applicable law. For India, processing is governed by the Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 (DPDP Act). For the UK/EU, processing complies with the UK GDPR and EU GDPR. For Kenya, processing complies with the Data Protection Act 2019. For US users, we comply with applicable state privacy laws including the CCPA/CPRA.",
  "legalPrivacyLegalBasisHeading": "2. Legal bases for processing",
  "legalPrivacyPolicy": "Privacy Policy",
  "legalPrivacyRetentionBody": "We retain personal data for as long as your account is active. On account deletion, we delete or anonymize personal data within 30 days, except where retention is required by law (e.g., billing records retained for 7 years for tax compliance, audit logs retained for 12 months). Firm tenants may configure custom retention policies up to 7 years via governance settings. AI-training datasets derived from opted-in content are subject to the retention schedule in our Data & AI Consent Policy.",
  "legalPrivacyRetentionHeading": "6. Retention",
  "legalPrivacyRightsCCPABody": "California (CCPA/CPRA) rights: right to know what personal information we collect; right to delete; right to opt out of sale (we do not sell data); right to non-discrimination for exercising rights; right to correct inaccurate information; right to limit use of sensitive personal information.",
  "legalPrivacyRightsDPDPBody": "India DPDP Act rights: right to access, correction, and erasure of your digital personal data; right to grievance redressal; right to nominate a person to exercise rights on your behalf. Contact our Consent Manager at support@odaflow.com.",
  "legalPrivacyRightsGDPRBody": "GDPR / UK GDPR rights (EU and UK users): access — obtain a copy of your personal data; rectification — correct inaccurate data; erasure — request deletion (subject to legal hold); restriction — limit processing while a dispute is resolved; portability — receive your data in a machine-readable format; objection — object to processing based on legitimate interests; automated decisions — not to be subject to solely automated decisions with significant effects. To exercise these rights, email support@odaflow.com or use the in-app privacy settings.",
  "legalPrivacyRightsHeading": "9. Your rights",
  "legalPrivacyRightsKenyaBody": "Kenya Data Protection Act rights: right to be informed; right of access; right to rectification; right to erasure and blocking; right to object; right to data portability. Contact our local representative at support@odaflow.com.",
  "legalPrivacySecurityBody": "We implement technical and organisational measures including: TLS 1.2+ encryption in transit; AES-256 encryption at rest; role-based access control with least-privilege principles; multi-factor authentication for administrative access; automated vulnerability scanning; penetration testing at least annually; and an incident response plan. In the event of a personal data breach affecting your rights, we will notify you within 72 hours of becoming aware, as required under applicable law.",
  "legalPrivacySecurityHeading": "7. Security",
  "legalPrivacySharingBody": "We do not sell your personal data. We share data only as follows:",
  "legalPrivacySharingHeading": "5. Who we share your data with",
  "legalPrivacySharingLawyerReview": "Lawyer review: if you request a lawyer review, your case summary (not full content unless you authorise it) is shared with the assigned licensed lawyer on our marketplace. You control what is shared.",
  "legalPrivacySharingLegal": "Legal disclosures: we may disclose data when required by law, court order, or regulatory authority, and will notify you unless legally prohibited from doing so.",
  "legalPrivacySharingSubprocessors": "Subprocessors: we engage third-party subprocessors under data-processing agreements that require equivalent protections. Key categories: (i) Cloud infrastructure — AWS (data hosted in the region closest to your country); (ii) Payment processing — Stripe; (iii) Error monitoring — Sentry; (iv) Analytics — Vercel; (v) AI model providers — OpenAI and DeepSeek (AI analysis and embeddings); Deepgram (meeting transcription) — queries are sent under zero-data-retention API agreements where available; (vi) Email delivery — Resend.",
  "legalPrivacyTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "legalPrivacyTransfersBody": "Your data may be processed outside your country of residence. For transfers from the UK/EU, we rely on Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission and UK ICO. For India, transfers comply with DPDP Act provisions on cross-border data flows. For Kenya, transfers comply with Section 48 of the Kenya Data Protection Act 2019. Enterprise tenants may request data residency restrictions via governance settings.",
  "legalPrivacyTransfersHeading": "10. International transfers",
  "legalPrivacyUseBody": "We use collected data to: (a) create and maintain your account; (b) deliver AI legal analysis, matter management, billing, research, and other platform features; (c) process payments and send invoices; (d) send transactional emails (account confirmation, password reset, billing receipts); (e) detect, investigate, and prevent fraud, security incidents, and abuse; (f) comply with legal obligations including court orders and regulatory requirements; (g) analyse aggregate platform usage to improve features (using anonymized or pseudonymized data only); (h) send marketing communications where you have opted in (you may withdraw consent at any time).",
  "legalPrivacyUseHeading": "4. How we use your information",
  "legalPublisherName": "DVTech Ventures",
  "legalStandardDisclaimer": "Umbrella provides legal information, document explanations, issue identification, and risk analysis. It is not a law firm and does not replace a licensed attorney. For legal advice specific to your situation, consult a qualified lawyer in your jurisdiction.",
  "legalTermsAIOutputsBody": "AI Outputs are generated by large language models and are provided for informational purposes only. They do not constitute legal advice, do not create an attorney-client relationship, and should not be relied upon as a substitute for advice from a qualified lawyer. AI Outputs may be incomplete, inaccurate, or out of date. Citations to statutes and cases must be independently verified. You are solely responsible for any action taken based on AI Outputs.",
  "legalTermsAIOutputsHeading": "9. Nature of AI Outputs",
  "legalTermsAccountBody": "You must provide accurate and complete registration information and keep it updated. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your credentials and for all activity under your account. You must notify us immediately of any unauthorised access at support@odaflow.com. We reserve the right to disable accounts that violate these Terms or that we reasonably suspect are compromised.",
  "legalTermsAccountHeading": "3. Account registration",
  "legalTermsAgreementBody": "By creating an account or using any Umbrella service, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you are using the platform on behalf of a law firm, company, or other legal entity, you represent that you have the authority to bind that entity. If you do not accept these Terms, you must not use the platform. Users must be at least 18 years old.",
  "legalTermsAgreementHeading": "1. Acceptance",
  "legalTermsChangesBody": "We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be notified by email and in-app notification at least 30 days before they take effect. Continued use after the effective date constitutes acceptance.",
  "legalTermsChangesHeading": "20. Changes to these Terms",
  "legalTermsConfidentialityBody": "We treat your content and matter data as confidential and will not disclose it to third parties except as described in our Privacy Policy or as required by law. Lawyer Users must ensure client-confidential communications comply with applicable professional privilege rules. Our systems are architected to isolate tenant data.",
  "legalTermsConfidentialityHeading": "13. Confidentiality",
  "legalTermsContactBody": "Questions about these Terms: support@odaflow.com. DVTech Ventures, registered office details available on request.",
  "legalTermsContactHeading": "21. Contact",
  "legalTermsDataBody": "Our collection and use of personal data is described in the Privacy Policy. AI training and analytics uses require explicit opt-in as described in the Data & AI Consent Policy.",
  "legalTermsDataConsentLink": "Data & AI Consent Policy",
  "legalTermsDataHeading": "15. Data and privacy",
  "legalTermsDataPrivacyLink": "Privacy Policy",
  "legalTermsDefinitionsBody": "\"Platform\" means umbrella.okaylegal.ai and all associated applications, APIs, and services. \"Consumer User\" means a natural person using the platform to understand their own legal situation. \"Lawyer User\" means a licensed legal professional using the Lawyer OS features. \"Tenant\" means a law firm or organisation with a firm subscription. \"AI Output\" means any text, analysis, draft, or recommendation generated by Umbrella's AI systems. \"Matter\" means a legal case or transaction managed through the Lawyer OS. \"DVTech Ventures\" or \"we\" means the operator of the platform.",
  "legalTermsDefinitionsHeading": "2. Definitions",
  "legalTermsDescription": "These Terms govern your use of Umbrella — the AI-native legal platform operated by DVTech Ventures. Please read them carefully before using any part of the platform.",
  "legalTermsDisputeBody": "India users: these Terms are governed by the laws of India; disputes shall be resolved by binding arbitration under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act 1996, seated in Bengaluru. United States users: disputes shall be resolved by binding arbitration under AAA Commercial Arbitration Rules, seated in Delaware; class action waiver applies. Kenya users: these Terms are governed by the laws of Kenya; disputes shall be resolved under the Nairobi Centre for International Arbitration (NCIA) rules. United Kingdom users: these Terms are governed by English law; disputes shall be submitted to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales. In all cases, nothing prevents you from seeking urgent injunctive relief from a competent court.",
  "legalTermsDisputeHeading": "18. Dispute resolution and governing law",
  "legalTermsIPContentBody": "You retain ownership of all content you submit to the platform. By submitting content you grant DVTech Ventures a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to process, store, and display your content solely to deliver the services. This licence does not extend to AI training unless you opt in under the Data & AI Consent Policy.",
  "legalTermsIPHeading": "12. Intellectual property",
  "legalTermsIPPlatformBody": "DVTech Ventures owns all rights in the Umbrella platform, brand, underlying AI models, and technology. You are granted a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the platform for the duration of your subscription.",
  "legalTermsIndemnityBody": "You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless DVTech Ventures and its officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any claims, damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from: (a) your use of the platform in violation of these Terms; (b) your violation of any applicable law; (c) content you submit that infringes a third party's rights; (d) legal advice or services you provide to your clients using the platform.",
  "legalTermsIndemnityHeading": "17. Indemnification",
  "legalTermsLawyerUsersBody": "Lawyer Users are independent licensed professionals. By using the Lawyer OS, you confirm that you hold a valid practising certificate in your jurisdiction and that you will use the platform in compliance with applicable professional conduct rules and bar regulations. You remain solely responsible for the quality and legality of all legal work and advice you provide to your clients. Umbrella provides tools — it does not supervise or guarantee the professional conduct of Lawyer Users.",
  "legalTermsLawyerUsersHeading": "11. Lawyer users",
  "legalTermsLiabilityBody": "TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW: (a) DVTECH VENTURES' TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO THESE TERMS OR THE PLATFORM IS LIMITED TO THE AMOUNT YOU PAID US IN THE 12 MONTHS PRECEDING THE CLAIM; (b) WE ARE NOT LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, LOSS OF PROFITS, LOSS OF DATA, OR LOSS OF GOODWILL. THESE LIMITATIONS APPLY EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES AND REGARDLESS OF THE LEGAL THEORY ASSERTED.",
  "legalTermsLiabilityHeading": "16. Limitation of liability",
  "legalTermsNotLawFirmBody": "Umbrella is a technology platform, not a law firm. DVTech Ventures does not provide legal advice or legal representation. Use of the platform does not create an attorney-client relationship between you and DVTech Ventures. The lawyer marketplace connects you with independent licensed lawyers; any engagement with a marketplace lawyer is governed by a separate retainer agreement between you and that lawyer.",
  "legalTermsNotLawFirmHeading": "10. Not a law firm",
  "legalTermsOfService": "Terms of Service",
  "legalTermsPermittedUseBody": "You may use the platform to: obtain AI-generated legal information for personal or professional use; manage legal matters, clients, billing, and documents (Lawyer OS); access the lawyer marketplace to connect with licensed attorneys; and integrate the platform with your systems via our documented API.",
  "legalTermsPermittedUseHeading": "4. Permitted use",
  "legalTermsProhibitedUseBody": "You must not: (a) impersonate a lawyer, judge, or government official; (b) use AI Outputs as formal legal advice to third parties without lawyer review; (c) submit unlawful, defamatory, or fraudulent content; (d) attempt to reverse-engineer, scrape, or extract the underlying AI models or training data; (e) resell or sublicense access to the platform without written consent; (f) use the platform in any way that violates applicable law, including data protection, consumer protection, and legal profession rules; (g) submit content that infringes third-party intellectual property rights.",
  "legalTermsProhibitedUseHeading": "5. Prohibited use",
  "legalTermsRefundBody": "You may cancel your subscription at any time from account settings. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period; no partial refunds are issued for unused time. If you believe you have been charged in error, contact support@odaflow.com within 30 days of the charge. We will review and, if appropriate, issue a pro-rata refund at our discretion.",
  "legalTermsRefundHeading": "8. Refunds and cancellation",
  "legalTermsSeverabilityBody": "If any provision of these Terms is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in full force. Our failure to enforce any right is not a waiver of that right. These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy and Data & AI Consent Policy, constitute the entire agreement between you and DVTech Ventures regarding the platform.",
  "legalTermsSeverabilityHeading": "19. General",
  "legalTermsSubscriptionBody": "Paid plans are billed in advance on a monthly or annual cycle. Prices are displayed in your local currency at checkout and may include applicable taxes. Subscriptions auto-renew at the end of each billing period unless you cancel before the renewal date. Failure to pay may result in suspension or termination of access.",
  "legalTermsSubscriptionHeading": "6. Subscriptions and billing",
  "legalTermsTitle": "Terms of Service",
  "legalTermsTrialBody": "Free trials are available for new accounts as specified at sign-up. At the end of the trial period, your account will automatically convert to a paid subscription at the applicable rate unless you cancel before the trial ends. We reserve the right to modify or discontinue trial offers at any time.",
  "legalTermsTrialHeading": "7. Free trials",
  "legalTermsWarrantiesBody": "We warrant that: (a) we will provide the platform with reasonable skill and care; (b) we will maintain commercially reasonable security practices. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE PLATFORM IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, OR UNINTERRUPTED AVAILABILITY. WE DO NOT WARRANT THE ACCURACY, COMPLETENESS, OR CURRENCY OF AI OUTPUTS.",
  "legalTermsWarrantiesHeading": "14. Warranties and disclaimers",
